add('My Extremely Biased Tier List','Long-form reading',6,section('Reading · First read',prompt('Read the complete article. What is the author ranking? Why do they make the list?')+`<div class="article"><div class="article-header"><div class="eyebrow">CULTURE / WEEKEND EDITION</div><h2>My Extremely Biased Tier List</h2><p>A ranking nobody asked for, but everyone will have an opinion about.</p></div><div class="article-body"><p>Every Friday, I promise myself I'm going to have the most productive weekend ever. There are <b>plenty of</b> places I could visit, <b>a few</b> friends I could meet, and <b>some</b> things around the house I really need to finish. Unfortunately, I work in IT, and lately I've <b>had a lot on my plate</b>. My phone <b>is always buzzing</b>, and I <b>keep getting sidetracked</b> by messages. So, when Saturday finally comes, I just want to <b>sleep in, switch off</b>, and <b>recharge</b>.</p><p>This weekend, instead of making another unrealistic plan, I've decided to rank the things I actually enjoy doing when I have <b>some downtime</b>.</p><h3>S TIER — STORY-DRIVEN GAMES</h3><p>For me, nothing beats a good story-driven game. I'm currently replaying <i>Detroit: Become Human</i>, and honestly, the storytelling is <b>on another level</b>. The characters are interesting, the choices feel important, and some scenes are <b>way better</b> than anything I've watched recently. The only problem? I always <b>get hooked</b> and <b>lose track of time</b>. I tell myself I'm only going to play for twenty minutes, but three hours later I'm still there. Absolutely <b>top-tier</b> entertainment.</p><h3>A TIER — FANFICTION</h3><p>I <b>have a soft spot for</b> ridiculously long Harry Potter fanfics, especially Drarry stories. Some are genuinely better written than published novels. Others are completely ridiculous, but that's part of the fun. Fanfiction can be <b>hit-or-miss</b>: sometimes the dialogue is amazing, but other times the romantic scenes <b>fall flat</b>. Still, good fanfiction is seriously <b>underrated</b>. Plus, there are plenty of free stories online, so I don't have to spend <b>much</b> money to enjoy myself.</p><h3>A TIER — CONCERT PERFORMANCES</h3><p>Sometimes I just want to <b>take it easy</b>, <b>grab a bite</b>, and watch an old concert recording. Michael Jackson's performances are absolutely <b>iconic</b>, and his dancing always <b>stands out</b>. Watching concerts online isn't quite as exciting as seeing an artist live, but it's still <b>worth it</b>.</p><h3>B TIER — MOVIE MARATHONS</h3><p>I enjoy <b>binge-watching</b> movies, but some franchises are becoming a bit <b>overrated</b>. Certain new releases don't <b>live up to the hype</b>, and their endings can be a huge <b>letdown</b>. There are still a few films I want to <b>catch up on</b>, though. Spending an afternoon watching something familiar is my <b>guilty pleasure</b>.</p><h3>F TIER — ENDLESS SCROLLING</h3><p>TikTok can be hilarious, but let's face it: a lot of content is pretty <b>mid</b>. I <b>tend to scroll through</b> videos when I'm bored, and suddenly an hour has disappeared. Sometimes I <b>come across</b> something genuinely funny, but <b>most of the time</b> I don't even remember what I've watched.</p><p><b>Final verdict:</b> My perfect day off doesn't need a complicated schedule. Just give me a comfortable sofa, <b>a little</b> food, <b>enough</b> free time, and something entertaining. And yes, I'm judging anyone who puts <i>Detroit: Become Human</i> in F tier.</p></div></div>`)+section('Gist check',radio('gist','Which best describes this article?',['Advice about becoming more productive','A personal ranking of free-time activities','A review of the Harry Potter franchise'],1)+checkbar()) ,'Reading');
