add('Rule 2 · Superlatives','Grammar with practice',3,section('Grammar card 2',`<div class="rule">${ruleTitle(2,'Superlatives: the whole group')}<p>We use the <b>superlative</b> to identify the strongest or weakest example in a group. Usually use <b>the</b>.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>Short adjective + <b>-est</b></td><td>small → the smallest</td></tr><tr><td>Consonant + y → <b>-iest</b></td><td>busy → the busiest</td></tr><tr><td>the most / least + longer adjective</td><td>the most exciting / the least relaxing</td></tr><tr><td>Irregular adjectives</td><td>the best / the worst</td></tr></table></div><div class="rule-example">“This is <b>the funniest</b> meme I’ve seen lately.”<br>“It’s <b>one of the best games</b> I’ve ever played.”</div><p>After <b>one of the + superlative</b>, use a <b>plural noun</b>: <i>one of the best performances</i>.</p></div>`)+qsection('Your turn · Complete 4 sentences',prompt('Use the correct superlative form.')+
