add('Rule 3 · Modifiers','Grammar with practice',3,section('Grammar card 3',`<div class="rule">${ruleTitle(3,'How big is the difference?')}<p>Use modifiers to show whether two things are <b>very different</b> or <b>only a little different</b>.</p><div class="grid2"><div class="soft"><b>Big difference</b><p>much / far / a lot / <b>way</b> (informal) + comparative</p><p>“This game is <b>way more interesting</b>.”</p></div><div class="soft"><b>Small difference</b><p>slightly / a bit / a little + comparative</p><p>“The second film is <b>slightly better</b>.”</p></div></div><p>Emphasise a superlative with <b>by far</b> or <b>easily</b>: “This is <b>by far the best</b> film.”</p><p class="micro">Say <i>much better</i>, not <i>very better</i>.</p></div>`)+qsection('Your turn · Complete 4 sentences',prompt('Use the words in brackets.')+
