add('Rule 4 · As ... as','Grammar with practice',3,section('Grammar card 4',`<div class="rule">${ruleTitle(4,'(Not) as ... as and quantity')}<p>Use <b>as + adjective + as</b> for equal degree. Use <b>not as ... as</b> when there is a difference.</p><div class="rule-example">“Staying in is <b>just as enjoyable as</b> going out.”<br>“The sequel isn’t <b>nearly as good as</b> the original.”</div><div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>just as ... as</td><td>exactly as ... as</td></tr><tr><td>almost as ... as</td><td>nearly equal</td></tr><tr><td>not quite as ... as</td><td>slightly less</td></tr><tr><td>not nearly as ... as</td><td>much less</td></tr><tr><td>as <b>many</b> ... as</td><td>countable plural nouns</td></tr><tr><td>as <b>much</b> ... as</td><td>uncountable nouns</td></tr></table></div></div>`)+qsection('Your turn · Complete 4 sentences',prompt('Use the words in brackets and add any necessary words.')+
