add('Grammar in Context','Story cloze',5,section('The Weekend Tier List',prompt('Read the story and choose the correct grammar for each numbered gap.')+`<div class="article"><div class="article-header"><div class="eyebrow">GRAMMAR / SHORT STORY</div><h2>The Weekend Tier List</h2><p>Choose the best form. Be careful: some options sound like internet English, but are grammatically incorrect.</p></div><div class="article-body cloze"><p>It was finally Saturday. After a long week at work, my phone was still buzzing, and I had a lot on my plate. But I finally had some downtime, so I decided to make ${choice('cl1',['gooder','better','the best','best'],2)} tier list of weekend plans for my group chat.</p><p>First, I compared staying in with going to a busy shopping centre. Staying in sounded ${choice('cl2',['most relaxing','more relaxing','relaxinger','relaxed'],1)} than walking around crowded shops, especially because I had only a little energy left.</p><p>My friend suggested watching a concert recording. I have a soft spot for Michael Jackson’s performances, and some of them are ${choice('cl3',['most better','the better','best','much better'],3)} than the random videos that appear on my For You Page. Still, watching a performance online isn’t ${choice('cl4',['more exciting as','most exciting than','nearly as exciting as','as more exciting as'],2)} seeing an artist live.</p><p>Next, I put story-driven games in S tier. There are a few games I’m trying to catch up on, and I keep getting sidetracked by new releases. The writing in <i>Detroit: Become Human</i> is often ${choice('cl5',['more interesting','most interesting','the interestingest','as interesting'],0)} than in most mobile games. The only problem is that I get hooked and lose track of time. A short puzzle game, however, is ${choice('cl6',['easiest','easier','more easy','the easiest'],1)} to finish than a long story-driven game.</p><p>I also thought about going out to grab a bite. I have ${choice('cl7',['most','the most','much','more'],3)} free time this weekend than last weekend, but I don’t want to spend too much money. A café near my flat is ${choice('cl8',['cheapest','more cheap','slightly cheaper','the cheap'],2)} than the expensive place we tried last month, so it goes in A tier.</p><p>Finally, I ranked my TikTok habits. Some clips are iconic, but most are pretty mid. Of all the ridiculous videos I’ve come across lately, one cat video was ${choice('cl9',['far funnier','by far the funniest','the more funny','funniest than'],1)}. Unfortunately, I keep scrolling even when I’m trying to switch off. That’s probably ${choice('cl10',['worst','worse','the worse','the worst'],3)} habit on my entire list. Time to recharge instead!</p></div></div>`+checkbar())+section('One quick question',open('cloze-reflect','Which of the choices in this story would you change?','I would put ... higher because...',1)),'Consolidation');
add('The Comment Section','Practical reactions',3,section('Social media · Comment battle',`<div class="speech-bubble"><div class="speaker">@movieaddict</div><p>“The newer Marvel movies are way better than the old ones. I’ve been catching up on them, and I’m hooked.”</p></div><div class="speech-bubble"><div class="speaker">@lazyweekends</div><p>“Going out on your day off is seriously overrated. There’s nothing better than staying in and switching off.”</p></div><div class="speech-bubble"><div class="speaker">@drarryforever</div><p>“Some Drarry fanfics are by far better than the films. I’m not taking that back.”</p></div>`)+section('React naturally',prompt('Choose a response to each comment, then explain your opinion out loud.')+radio('react1','What would you reply to @movieaddict?',['I couldn’t agree more.','I see your point, but...','That’s a terrible take!'],null)+radio('react2','What would you reply to @lazyweekends?',['To be fair, that depends on the day.','That is a scientifically impossible claim.','I have no personal preferences.'],null)+open('react-open','Write one short internet-style reply. Include an old vocabulary phrase.','To be fair, I tend to...',2)),'Extra practice');
add('Fix This Terrible Review','Editing challenge',3,qsection('Find the errors',prompt('This reviewer thinks the game is mid, but their English is even worse. Pick the correct replacement for each error.')+`<div class="speech-bubble"><div class="speaker">@reviewer404</div><p>“I have a soft spot for story-driven games, but this one is <b>more worse</b> than I expected. The characters are <b>the most boringest</b> I’ve seen. There <b>isn’t as many</b> interesting choices as in Detroit. The ending is <b>not nearly as better as</b> the beginning. I’m <b>usually getting hooked</b> on games like this, but this one was a letdown.”</p></div>`+radio('fix1','1. “more worse”',['more bad','much worse','most worse'],1)+radio('fix2','2. “the most boringest”',['the most boring','the boringest more','the most boringer'],0)+radio('fix3','3. “isn’t as many”',['aren’t as many','isn’t as much','are not much'],0)+radio('fix4','4. “not nearly as better as”',['not nearly as best as','not nearly as good as','not nearly better as'],1)+radio('fix5','5. “usually getting hooked”',['usually get hooked','am usually get hooked','usually hooked getting'],0)),'Extra practice');
add('Guess Who?','Quick guessing card',1,section('Guess the character, artist or activity',`<div class="grid3"><div class="card tint"><span class="chip">A</span><p>One of the most iconic performers ever. His dancing stands out, and fans still catch up on his old live performances.</p></div><div class="card tint"><span class="chip">B</span><p>A blond wizard. Some people can’t stand him, but others have a soft spot for him. He’s extremely popular in fanfiction.</p></div><div class="card tint"><span class="chip">C</span><p>People tend to do this when they have some downtime. They can lose track of time and stay up way too late.</p></div></div>`)+section('Your turn',prompt('Describe two things without naming them. Use a comparison and an expression from a previous lesson.')+open('guess','Write your two secret descriptions, or explain them aloud.','My first mystery is ...',3)),'Extra practice');
add('The Tier List Battle','Final speaking task',6,section('Create your ranking',`<div class="hero" style="min-height:155px"><h2>Your ranking. Your rules.</h2><p>Choose 6–8 movies, games, artists, hobbies or completely random things. Put them into tiers and defend your choices.</p></div><div class="tier-editor" id="tierEditor"></div><div class="rank-inputs"><input id="rankNew" placeholder="Add a character, game, song..." maxlength="60" aria-label="New tier item"><select id="rankTier" aria-label="Tier"><option>S</option><option>A</option><option>B</option><option>C</option><option>F</option></select><button id="addTierItem" type="button">+ Add</button></div><p class="micro">Tap a tier on each card to move it, or remove and add it again. This ranking is saved on your device.</p>`)+section('Now defend it',`<div class="grid2"><div class="soft"><b>Grammar challenge</b><p>✓ 3 comparatives<br>✓ 1 superlative<br>✓ 1 as...as comparison</p></div><div class="soft"><b>Vocabulary challenge</b><p>✓ 4 new ranking expressions<br>✓ 2 expressions from previous lessons</p></div></div><div class="soft">“I have a soft spot for...” · “It’s <b>way better than</b>...” · “It doesn’t <b>live up to the hype</b>.” · “This is <b>by far the best</b>...” · “To be fair...”</div><p><b>Teacher:</b> challenge two choices and ask for explanations.</p>${open('final-notes','Speaking notes (optional)','My S tier is ... because ...',3)}`),'Speaking');
add('Reflection & Homework','Wrap-up',2,section('Can-do reflection',prompt('Tick what you can do now.')+`<div class="soft" id="reflectChecks"><label><input type="checkbox" data-reflect="a" ${state.answers['reflect-a']?'checked':''}> Compare two things naturally</label><br><label><input type="checkbox" data-reflect="b" ${state.answers['reflect-b']?'checked':''}> Explain why something is the best or worst</label><br><label><input type="checkbox" data-reflect="c" ${state.answers['reflect-c']?'checked':''}> Make comparisons stronger or weaker</label><br><label><input type="checkbox" data-reflect="d" ${state.answers['reflect-d']?'checked':''}> React to another person’s ranking</label></div>${open('reflect-text','The most useful expression today was...','I can now say...',1)}`)+section('Homework · 20–25 minutes',`<div class="homework-card"><strong>01 / Vocabulary recall</strong><p>Write 6 natural comments using expressions from today. Include at least 3 phrases from earlier lessons: <i>get sidetracked, switch off, have a lot on my plate, catch up on, take it easy, lose track of time, a few, plenty of...</i></p></div><div class="homework-card"><strong>02 / Grammar in use</strong><p>Finish any uncompleted grammar cards, then write 5 comparisons about real things you like.</p></div><div class="homework-card"><strong>03 / New video input</strong><p>Watch another short film, game or music ranking video in English. Note 3 useful reactions or comparison phrases and explain them in your own words.</p></div><div class="homework-card"><strong>04 / Writing · 130–160 words</strong><p><b>My Most Controversial Ranking.</b> Choose three things you consider overrated, underrated or iconic. Explain why. Use 4 comparison structures, 5 expressions from today and 3 from previous lessons.</p></div>`)+note('All answers are saved locally in this browser. The YouTube video requires internet; the rest of the lesson works offline.') ,'Wrap-up');
// ───────────────────────────────── ENGINE ─────────────────────────────────
function idsInCurrentPage(){const box=document.getElementById('content');return [...new Set([...box.querySelectorAll('[data-quiz]')].map(e=>e.dataset.quiz))].filter(x=>keys[x]?.correct!==null&&keys[x]?.correct!==undefined)}
function evaluate(id){const q=keys[id];if(!q||q.correct===null||q.correct===undefined)return null;const a=state.answers[id];if(a===undefined||a==='')return null;return q.type==='gap' ? (Array.isArray(q.correct)?q.correct:[q.correct]).some(v=>norm(a)===norm(v)) : String(a)===String(q.correct)}
function paint(){
 const root=document.getElementById('content');
 for(const id of idsInCurrentPage()){
  const q=keys[id],correct=evaluate(id),marked=!!state.checked[id];
  const wrapper=root.querySelector(`[data-quiz="${id}"]`),feedback=root.querySelector(`[data-feedback="${id}"]`);
  if(!wrapper)continue;
  wrapper.querySelectorAll('.answer-option').forEach((option,i)=>{
   option.classList.toggle('is-right',marked&&i===q.correct&&correct!==null);
   option.classList.toggle('is-wrong',marked&&option.querySelector('input')?.checked&&i!==q.correct);
  });
  if(wrapper.matches('select,input')){
   wrapper.classList.toggle('is-right',marked&&correct===true);
   wrapper.classList.toggle('is-wrong',marked&&correct===false);
  }else{
   const field=wrapper.querySelector('input[type=text]');
   if(field){field.classList.toggle('is-right',marked&&correct===true);field.classList.toggle('is-wrong',marked&&correct===false)}
  }
  if(feedback){
   feedback.className='feedback';
   feedback.textContent='';
   if(marked&&correct!==null){feedback.classList.add(correct?'good':'bad');feedback.textContent=correct?'✓ Correct!':'Try again.'}
  }
 }
}
function checkPage(){const ids=idsInCurrentPage();let attempted=0,correct=0;for(const id of ids){const result=evaluate(id);if(result!==null){attempted++;state.checked[id]=true;if(result)correct++}}save();paint();const node=document.querySelector('[data-page-result]');if(node)node.textContent=`${correct} correct out of ${attempted} answered · ${ids.length} questions`}
function renderNav(){const nav=document.getElementById('nav');nav.innerHTML=pages.map((p,i)=>`<button type="button" data-page="${i}" class="nav-link ${i===page?'active':''} ${state.visited[i]?'done':''}"><span class="nav-no">${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><span class="nav-title">${esc(p.title)}</span></button>`).join('');nav.querySelector('.active')?.scrollIntoView({block:'nearest'});}
function render(){page=Math.min(Math.max(page,0),pages.length-1);state.page=page;state.visited[page]=1;save();const p=pages[page];document.getElementById('pageIntro').innerHTML=`<h1 class="page-title">${esc(p.title)}</h1>`;document.getElementById('content').innerHTML=`<div class="surface">${p.html}</div>`;document.getElementById('counter').textContent=`${page+1} / ${pages.length}`;document.getElementById('prev').disabled=page===0;document.getElementById('next').textContent=page===pages.length-1?(state.finished?'Completed ✓':'Finish lesson ✓'):'Next →';renderNav();paint();if(document.getElementById('tierEditor'))renderTier();window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'instant'})}
function navigate(n){page=Math.max(0,Math.min(n,pages.length-1));render();document.getElementById('rail').classList.remove('open')}
const tierColors={S:'#dfadae',A:'#edd2a1',B:'#d6e1ae',C:'#b4cadd',F:'#d3bdd6'};
function renderTier(){const root=document.getElementById('tierEditor');if(!root)return;root.innerHTML=['S','A','B','C','F'].map(t=>`<div class="tier-row"><div class="tier-label" style="background:${tierColors[t]}">${t}<small>${{S:'ICONIC',A:'LOVE IT',B:'SOLID',C:'MID',F:'NOPE'}[t]}</small></div><div class="tier-content">${state.tierItems.map((x,i)=>x.tier===t?`<span class="rank-chip">${esc(x.name)} <select aria-label="Move ${esc(x.name)}" data-tier-move="${i}" style="border:0;background:transparent;color:#7a667b;font-size:12px"><option value="">Move</option>${['S','A','B','C','F'].filter(y=>y!==t).map(y=>`<option value="${y}">${y}</option>`).join('')}</select><button data-tier-delete="${i}" type="button" aria-label="Remove ${esc(x.name)}">×</button></span>`:'').join('')||'<span class="micro">Add something here...</span>'}</div></div>`).join('')}
document.addEventListener('input',e=>{if(e.target.dataset.input){state.answers[e.target.dataset.input]=e.target.value;state.checked[e.target.dataset.input]=false;save()} });
document.addEventListener('change',e=>{if(e.target.dataset.radio){state.answers[e.target.dataset.radio]=e.target.value;state.checked[e.target.dataset.radio]=false;save();paint()}if(e.target.dataset.choice){state.answers[e.target.dataset.choice]=e.target.value;state.checked[e.target.dataset.choice]=false;save();paint()}if(e.target.dataset.reflect){state.answers['reflect-'+e.target.dataset.reflect]=e.target.checked;save()}if(e.target.dataset.tierMove){const idx=+e.target.dataset.tierMove;if(e.target.value){state.tierItems[idx].tier=e.target.value;save();renderTier()}}});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{const p=e.target.closest('[data-page]');if(p){navigate(+p.dataset.page);return}if(e.target.closest('[data-checkpage]')){checkPage();return}const del=e.target.closest('[data-tier-delete]');if(del){state.tierItems.splice(+del.dataset.tierDelete,1);save();renderTier();return}if(e.target.closest('#addTierItem')){const el=document.getElementById('rankNew'),name=el?.value.trim(),tier=document.getElementById('rankTier')?.value;if(name&&state.tierItems.length<30){state.tierItems.push({name,tier});el.value='';save();renderTier()}return}});
document.getElementById('prev').onclick=()=>navigate(page-1);document.getElementById('next').onclick=()=>{if(page===pages.length-1){state.finished=true;save();render();return}navigate(page+1)};document.getElementById('menu').onclick=()=>document.getElementById('rail').classList.toggle('open');document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Escape'){document.getElementById('rail').classList.remove('open')}if(e.key==='Enter'&&e.target.id==='rankNew')document.getElementById('addTierItem')?.click()});
render();
</script>
</body></html>
